From cb25899a403d2d81f016e49c8514a11d77d45b0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tung Son Do <dosontung007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:27:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): add --no-context-files to skip instruction files

A session started with --no-context-files loads no context files: no
AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md or other instruction file from the working folder,
its parents or additional workspace roots, at startup or on any prompt
rebuild. Subagents inherit the switch. --no-rules covers rules folders;
this covers the context-file capability, which no flag could turn off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
